[{"id":"mata-87-13-2","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umire","en":"he dies"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"},{"bs":"umiremo","en":"we die"},{"bs":"umrli su","en":"they died"}],"ref":"87:13","answerWord":"يَمُوتُ","answerSound":"audio/0d63b367e56cdae34d34.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Wherein he will neither die nor live.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["ثُمَّ","لَا","يَمُوتُ","فِيهَا","وَلَا","يَحْيَىٰ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-9-125-9","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"i umrli su","en":"and they died"},{"bs":"umro sam","en":"I died"},{"bs":"umire","en":"he dies"},{"bs":"umro si","en":"you died"}],"ref":"9:125","answerWord":"وَمَاتُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/e3273a8ea245d105ac2a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But as for those in whose hearts is disease, it only addeth wickedness to their wickedness, and they die while they are disbelievers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَأَمَّا","ٱلَّذِينَ","فِى","قُلُوبِهِم","مَّرَضٌ","فَزَادَتْهُمْ","رِجْسًا","إِلَىٰ","رِجْسِهِمْ","وَمَاتُوا۟","وَهُمْ","كَٰفِرُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-2-243-14","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"},{"bs":"i umrli su","en":"and they died"},{"bs":"umro si","en":"you died"},{"bs":"umrete","en":"you die"}],"ref":"2:243","answerWord":"مُوتُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/11d10c02c6991f3a234d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Bethink thee (O Muhammad) of those of old, who went forth from their habitations in their thousands, fearing death, and Allah said unto them: Die; and then He brought them back to life. Lo! Allah is a Lord of Kindness to mankind, but most of mankind give not thanks.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["أَلَمْ","تَرَ","إِلَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","خَرَجُوا۟","مِن","دِيَٰرِهِمْ","وَهُمْ","أُلُوفٌ","حَذَرَ","ٱلْمَوْتِ","فَقَالَ","لَهُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","مُوتُوا۟","ثُمَّ","أَحْيَٰهُمْ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","لَذُو","فَضْلٍ","عَلَى","ٱلنَّاسِ","وَلَٰكِنَّ","أَكْثَرَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","لَا","يَشْكُرُونَ"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-3-144-10","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umro je","en":"he/it died"},{"bs":"pa umire","en":"so he/it dies"},{"bs":"umrete","en":"you die"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"}],"ref":"3:144","answerWord":"مَّاتَ","answerSound":"audio/ebf35b2d64beb85b64e6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Muhammad is but a messenger, messengers (the like of whom) have passed away before him. Will it be that, when he dieth or is slain, ye will turn back on your heels? He who turneth back on his heels doth no hurt to Allah, and Allah will reward the thankful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَمَا","مُحَمَّدٌ","إِلَّا","رَسُولٌ","قَدْ","خَلَتْ","مِن","قَبْلِهِ","ٱلرُّسُلُ","أَفَإِي۟ن","مَّاتَ","أَوْ","قُتِلَ","ٱنقَلَبْتُمْ","عَلَىٰٓ","أَعْقَٰبِكُمْ","وَمَن","يَنقَلِبْ","عَلَىٰ","عَقِبَيْهِ","فَلَن","يَضُرَّ","ٱللَّهَ","شَيْـًٔا","وَسَيَجْزِى","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-19-66-4","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umro sam","en":"I died"},{"bs":"umro si","en":"you died"},{"bs":"pa umire","en":"so he/it dies"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"}],"ref":"19:66","answerWord":"مِتُّ","answerSound":"audio/cb638d5db2c45715d7ce.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And man saith: When I am dead, shall I forsooth be brought forth alive?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَيَقُولُ","ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ","أَءِذَا","مَا","مِتُّ","لَسَوْفَ","أُخْرَجُ","حَيًّا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-23-37-5","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umiremo","en":"we die"},{"bs":"umirem","en":"I die"},{"bs":"umirete","en":"you (all) die"},{"bs":"umro sam","en":"I died"}],"ref":"23:37","answerWord":"نَمُوتُ","answerSound":"audio/d38a2c4a9cd6ad069805.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"There is naught but our life of the world; we die and we live, and we shall not be raised (again).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["إِنْ","هِىَ","إِلَّا","حَيَاتُنَا","ٱلدُّنْيَا","نَمُوتُ","وَنَحْيَا","وَمَا","نَحْنُ","بِمَبْعُوثِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-3-157-6","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umrli ste","en":"you (all) died"},{"bs":"umro je","en":"he/it died"},{"bs":"umrli su","en":"they died"},{"bs":"umro sam","en":"I died"}],"ref":"3:157","answerWord":"مُتُّمْ","answerSound":"audio/87ba818669f82a280038.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And what though ye be slain in Allah's way or die therein? Surely pardon from Allah and mercy are better than all that they amass.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَلَئِن","قُتِلْتُمْ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","أَوْ","مُتُّمْ","لَمَغْفِرَةٌ","مِّنَ","ٱللَّهِ","وَرَحْمَةٌ","خَيْرٌ","مِّمَّا","يَجْمَعُونَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-3-158-1","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umrete","en":"you die"},{"bs":"umrli su","en":"they died"},{"bs":"umiremo","en":"we die"},{"bs":"umro sam","en":"I died"}],"ref":"3:158","answerWord":"مُّتُّمْ","answerSound":"audio/f1fc17a2305ab9ed631e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"What though ye be slain or die, when unto Allah ye are gathered?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَلَئِن","مُّتُّمْ","أَوْ","قُتِلْتُمْ","لَإِلَى","ٱللَّهِ","تُحْشَرُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-4-18-16","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umiru","en":"they die"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"},{"bs":"umirem","en":"I die"},{"bs":"umrli ste","en":"you (all) died"}],"ref":"4:18","answerWord":"يَمُوتُونَ","answerSound":"audio/700c68587ffedc5f1320.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The forgiveness is not for those who do ill-deeds until, when death attendeth upon one of them, he saith: Lo! I repent now; nor yet for those who die while they are disbelievers. For such We have prepared a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَلَيْسَتِ","ٱلتَّوْبَةُ","لِلَّذِينَ","يَعْمَلُونَ","ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ","حَتَّىٰٓ","إِذَا","حَضَرَ","أَحَدَهُمُ","ٱلْمَوْتُ","قَالَ","إِنِّى","تُبْتُ","ٱلْـَٰٔنَ","وَلَا","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَمُوتُونَ","وَهُمْ","كُفَّارٌ","أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","أَعْتَدْنَا","لَهُمْ","عَذَابًا","أَلِيمًا"],"marked":[16],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-7-25-4","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umirete","en":"you (all) die"},{"bs":"pa umire","en":"so he/it dies"},{"bs":"i umrli su","en":"and they died"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"}],"ref":"7:25","answerWord":"تَمُوتُونَ","answerSound":"audio/9967557b05cddaeb4a26.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He said: There shall ye live, and there shall ye die, and thence shall ye be brought forth.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["قَالَ","فِيهَا","تَحْيَوْنَ","وَفِيهَا","تَمُوتُونَ","وَمِنْهَا","تُخْرَجُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-19-33-5","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umirem","en":"I die"},{"bs":"umrete","en":"you die"},{"bs":"umrite!","en":"(you all) die!"},{"bs":"pa umire","en":"so he/it dies"}],"ref":"19:33","answerWord":"أَمُوتُ","answerSound":"audio/259baf76c16679d8f495.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Peace on me the day I was born, and the day I die, and the day I shall be raised alive!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَٱلسَّلَٰمُ","عَلَىَّ","يَوْمَ","وُلِدتُّ","وَيَوْمَ","أَمُوتُ","وَيَوْمَ","أُبْعَثُ","حَيًّا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"mata-21-34-7","words":["verb:mata"],"options":[{"bs":"umro si","en":"you died"},{"bs":"umrli ste","en":"you (all) died"},{"bs":"umirem","en":"I die"},{"bs":"umro je","en":"he/it died"}],"ref":"21:34","answerWord":"مِّتَّ","answerSound":"audio/86524046d4c1ecde7c56.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We appointed immortality for no mortal before thee. What! if thou diest, can they be immortal!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"umrijeti","en":"to die"},"passage":["وَمَا","جَعَلْنَا","لِبَشَرٍ","مِّن","قَبْلِكَ","ٱلْخُلْدَ","أَفَإِي۟ن","مِّتَّ","فَهُمُ","ٱلْخَٰلِدُونَ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"ماتَ"}},{"id":"kariha-8-8-5","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"mrzili","en":"disliked"},{"bs":"mrzite","en":"you (all) dislike"},{"bs":"mrzili ste ih","en":"you (all) disliked them"},{"bs":"i mrzili su","en":"and they disliked"}],"ref":"8:8","answerWord":"كَرِهَ","answerSound":"audio/44ee578a402d5d572b0d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"That He might cause the Truth to triumph and bring vanity to naught, however much the guilty might oppose;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["لِيُحِقَّ","ٱلْحَقَّ","وَيُبْطِلَ","ٱلْبَٰطِلَ","وَلَوْ","كَرِهَ","ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"kariha-2-216-8","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"mrzite","en":"you (all) dislike"},{"bs":"mrze","en":"they dislike"},{"bs":"pa ste se toga gnušali","en":"so you (all) detested it"},{"bs":"mrzili","en":"disliked"}],"ref":"2:216","answerWord":"تَكْرَهُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/d85275d923f7f08093ce.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Warfare is ordained for you, though it is hateful unto you; but it may happen that ye hate a thing which is good for you, and it may happen that ye love a thing which is bad for you. Allah knoweth, ye know not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["كُتِبَ","عَلَيْكُمُ","ٱلْقِتَالُ","وَهُوَ","كُرْهٌ","لَّكُمْ","وَعَسَىٰٓ","أَن","تَكْرَهُوا۟","شَيْـًٔا","وَهُوَ","خَيْرٌ","لَّكُمْ","وَعَسَىٰٓ","أَن","تُحِبُّوا۟","شَيْـًٔا","وَهُوَ","شَرٌّ","لَّكُمْ","وَٱللَّهُ","يَعْلَمُ","وَأَنتُمْ","لَا","تَعْلَمُونَ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"kariha-47-9-2","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"mrzili su","en":"they disliked"},{"bs":"mrzili ste ih","en":"you (all) disliked them"},{"bs":"pa ste se toga gnušali","en":"so you (all) detested it"},{"bs":"mrze","en":"they dislike"}],"ref":"47:9","answerWord":"كَرِهُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/bb089b569a05758bee3e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"That is because they are averse to that which Allah hath revealed, therefor maketh He their actions fruitless.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["ذَٰلِكَ","بِأَنَّهُمْ","كَرِهُوا۟","مَآ","أَنزَلَ","ٱللَّهُ","فَأَحْبَطَ","أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"kariha-9-81-6","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"i mrzili su","en":"and they disliked"},{"bs":"mrze","en":"they dislike"},{"bs":"pa ste se toga gnušali","en":"so you (all) detested it"},{"bs":"mrzite","en":"you (all) dislike"}],"ref":"9:81","answerWord":"وَكَرِهُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/2cad6655e5dfafd7ea1e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Those who were left behind rejoiced at sitting still behind the messenger of Allah, and were averse to striving with their wealth and their lives in Allah's way. And they said: Go not forth in the heat! Say: The fire of hell is more intense of heat, if they but understood.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["فَرِحَ","ٱلْمُخَلَّفُونَ","بِمَقْعَدِهِمْ","خِلَٰفَ","رَسُولِ","ٱللَّهِ","وَكَرِهُوٓا۟","أَن","يُجَٰهِدُوا۟","بِأَمْوَٰلِهِمْ","وَأَنفُسِهِمْ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","وَقَالُوا۟","لَا","تَنفِرُوا۟","فِى","ٱلْحَرِّ","قُلْ","نَارُ","جَهَنَّمَ","أَشَدُّ","حَرًّا","لَّوْ","كَانُوا۟","يَفْقَهُونَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"kariha-16-62-3","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"mrze","en":"they dislike"},{"bs":"mrzili su","en":"they disliked"},{"bs":"mrzili","en":"disliked"},{"bs":"pa ste se toga gnušali","en":"so you (all) detested it"}],"ref":"16:62","answerWord":"يَكْرَهُونَ","answerSound":"audio/93423727aa3a1ebdddf6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they assign unto Allah that which they (themselves) dislike, and their tongues expound the lie that the better portion will be theirs. Assuredly theirs will be the Fire, and they will be abandoned.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["وَيَجْعَلُونَ","لِلَّهِ","مَا","يَكْرَهُونَ","وَتَصِفُ","أَلْسِنَتُهُمُ","ٱلْكَذِبَ","أَنَّ","لَهُمُ","ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ","لَا","جَرَمَ","أَنَّ","لَهُمُ","ٱلنَّارَ","وَأَنَّهُم","مُّفْرَطُونَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"kariha-47-28-6","words":["verb:kariha"],"options":[{"bs":"i mrzili su","en":"and they disliked"},{"bs":"mrze","en":"they dislike"},{"bs":"mrzite","en":"you (all) dislike"},{"bs":"mrzili","en":"disliked"}],"ref":"47:28","answerWord":"وَكَرِهُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/ef8fe2cd403f1926536f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"That will be because they followed that which angereth Allah, and hated that which pleaseth Him. Therefor He hath made their actions vain.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ne voljeti, mrziti","en":"to dislike, to hate"},"passage":["ذَٰلِكَ","بِأَنَّهُمُ","ٱتَّبَعُوا۟","مَآ","أَسْخَطَ","ٱللَّهَ","وَكَرِهُوا۟","رِضْوَٰنَهُۥ","فَأَحْبَطَ","أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"كَرِهَ"}},{"id":"qaada-7-16-3","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"zaista ću sjediti","en":"I will surely sit"},{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"},{"bs":"sjedimo","en":"we sit"},{"bs":"pa sjedite!","en":"so (you all) sit!"}],"ref":"7:16","answerWord":"لَأَقْعُدَنَّ","answerSound":"audio/1187b6a9736c190e213b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He said: Now, because Thou hast sent me astray, verily I shall lurk in ambush for them on Thy Right Path.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["قَالَ","فَبِمَآ","أَغْوَيْتَنِى","لَأَقْعُدَنَّ","لَهُمْ","صِرَٰطَكَ","ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}},{"id":"qaada-9-5-10","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"i vrebajte!","en":"and (you all) lie in wait!"},{"bs":"sjedite","en":"you (all) sit"},{"bs":"zaista ću sjediti","en":"I will surely sit"},{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"}],"ref":"9:5","answerWord":"وَٱقْعُدُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/a73d48d2d356895ade3a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then, when the sacred months have passed, slay the idolaters wherever ye find them, and take them (captive), and besiege them, and prepare for them each ambush. But if they repent and establish worship and pay the poor-due, then leave their way free. Lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["فَإِذَا","ٱنسَلَخَ","ٱلْأَشْهُرُ","ٱلْحُرُمُ","فَٱقْتُلُوا۟","ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ","حَيْثُ","وَجَدتُّمُوهُمْ","وَخُذُوهُمْ","وَٱحْصُرُوهُمْ","وَٱقْعُدُوا۟","لَهُمْ","كُلَّ","مَرْصَدٍ","فَإِن","تَابُوا۟","وَأَقَامُوا۟","ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ","وَءَاتَوُا۟","ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ","فَخَلُّوا۟","سَبِيلَهُمْ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}},{"id":"qaada-9-46-12","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"sjedite!","en":"(you all) sit!"},{"bs":"zaista ću sjediti","en":"I will surely sit"},{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"},{"bs":"sjedimo","en":"we sit"}],"ref":"9:46","answerWord":"ٱقْعُدُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/1aa7af217f87726f91ec.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if they had wished to go forth they would assuredly have made ready some equipment, but Allah was averse to their being sent forth and held them back and it was said (unto them): Sit ye with the sedentary!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["وَلَوْ","أَرَادُوا۟","ٱلْخُرُوجَ","لَأَعَدُّوا۟","لَهُۥ","عُدَّةً","وَلَٰكِن","كَرِهَ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱنۢبِعَاثَهُمْ","فَثَبَّطَهُمْ","وَقِيلَ","ٱقْعُدُوا۟","مَعَ","ٱلْقَٰعِدِينَ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}},{"id":"qaada-9-83-22","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"pa sjedite!","en":"so (you all) sit!"},{"bs":"zaista ću sjediti","en":"I will surely sit"},{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"},{"bs":"sjedimo","en":"we sit"}],"ref":"9:83","answerWord":"فَٱقْعُدُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/eb6fc60ae8227392c5f1.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"If Allah bring thee back (from the campaign) unto a party of them and they ask of thee leave to go out (to fight), then say unto them: Ye shall never more go out with me nor fight with me against a foe. Ye were content with sitting still the first time. So sit still, with the useless.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["فَإِن","رَّجَعَكَ","ٱللَّهُ","إِلَىٰ","طَآئِفَةٍ","مِّنْهُمْ","فَٱسْتَـْٔذَنُوكَ","لِلْخُرُوجِ","فَقُل","لَّن","تَخْرُجُوا۟","مَعِىَ","أَبَدًا","وَلَن","تُقَٰتِلُوا۟","مَعِىَ","عَدُوًّا","إِنَّكُمْ","رَضِيتُم","بِٱلْقُعُودِ","أَوَّلَ","مَرَّةٍ","فَٱقْعُدُوا۟","مَعَ","ٱلْخَٰلِفِينَ"],"marked":[22],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}},{"id":"qaada-9-90-6","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"},{"bs":"i vrebajte!","en":"and (you all) lie in wait!"},{"bs":"sjedite","en":"you (all) sit"},{"bs":"sjedimo","en":"we sit"}],"ref":"9:90","answerWord":"وَقَعَدَ","answerSound":"audio/3edb16542b326449bda4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And those among the wandering Arabs who had an excuse came in order that permission might be granted them. And those who lied to Allah and His messenger sat at home. A painful doom will fall on those of them who disbelieve.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["وَجَآءَ","ٱلْمُعَذِّرُونَ","مِنَ","ٱلْأَعْرَابِ","لِيُؤْذَنَ","لَهُمْ","وَقَعَدَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَذَبُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","وَرَسُولَهُۥ","سَيُصِيبُ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","مِنْهُمْ","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}},{"id":"qaada-72-9-2","words":["verb:qaada"],"options":[{"bs":"sjedimo","en":"we sit"},{"bs":"i sjeo je","en":"and he/it sat"},{"bs":"pa sjedite!","en":"so (you all) sit!"},{"bs":"zaista ću sjediti","en":"I will surely sit"}],"ref":"72:9","answerWord":"نَقْعُدُ","answerSound":"audio/f4bccc59b3a970b87a63.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And we used to sit on places (high) therein to listen. But he who listeneth now findeth a flame in wait for him;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"sjesti, sjediti","en":"to sit"},"passage":["وَأَنَّا","كُنَّا","نَقْعُدُ","مِنْهَا","مَقَٰعِدَ","لِلسَّمْعِ","فَمَن","يَسْتَمِعِ","ٱلْءَانَ","يَجِدْ","لَهُۥ","شِهَابًا","رَّصَدًا"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"قَعَدَ"}}]